></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c29\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2264\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c37\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>7</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span>. Justify your answer.</li>\n<li>Which properties of <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"m \\times m\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D45A TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-cD7\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D45A TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>×</mo><mi>m</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span>\nmatrices does the proof of <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"thm-strassen\">@thm-strassen</span> use? Say what would go\nwrong if the identity had needed two blocks to commute.</li>\n<li>State the difference between the error bound of <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"prp-classical-product-entrywise\">@prp-classical-product-entrywise</span>\nand that of <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"prp-strassen-norm-bound\">@prp-strassen-norm-bound</span>,\nand say for which matrices the difference matters.</li>\n</ol>\n</div>","file":"ch24-applied/13-fast-matrix-multiplication.html"}